// ============================================================================
// Harmonic PRZ Matrix Scanner — Gartley / Bat / Butterfly / Crab
// TradingView Pine Script v6 STRATEGY (not a plain indicator)
//
// Reference implementation for PRD.md §1.6, §3, §5–§7, §11 (Phase 1).
// Every ratio, invalidation, stop and target below is taken verbatim from the
// PRD's corrected §3.2 table — NOT from the original design brief, which
// contained the bugs this script deliberately avoids:
//   - no BC projection / AB=CD checks              -> added here (§3.2)
//   - Butterfly/Crab stop = own PRZ edge (0 buffer) -> stopR extends past it
//   - "1.130 XA" stop applied to all patterns        -> stop ratio is per-pattern
//   - targets measured off the CD leg                -> targets are on the AD leg
//   - blind limit order at D                         -> requires a confirmation
//                                                        candle inside the zone
//
// WHY A strategy() AND NOT AN indicator()
//   A strategy() is what makes historical validation real rather than asserted:
//   TradingView's own Strategy Tester replays this script's strategy.entry /
//   strategy.exit calls across every historical bar on whatever chart you load
//   it onto, and reports win rate, profit factor, drawdown and a full trade
//   list computed from THIS code, not from a claim in a document.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SIGNAL FUNNEL (read this before concluding "it doesn't work")
//   Stage 1  shape      B and C ratios land in a pattern's window (§3.2)
//   Stage 2  zone       price reaches the computed PRZ -> the zone ARMS
//   Stage 3  confirm    within `confirmBars` bars, a confirmation candle prints
//   Stage 4  gate       R:R to TP2 >= rrMin (§7.6)  -> trade fires
//   The on-chart table reports Zone (stage 2) and Trades (stage 4) separately,
//   so you can see WHICH stage is filtering, rather than guessing.
//
// TWO DESIGN BUGS FIXED IN THIS REVISION — both made signals multiplicatively
// rarer than the spec intends, and together explain near-zero trade counts
// across BTCUSDT / ETHUSD / ADAUSDT / NBIX / PFE / AZTA daily histories:
//   1. CONFIRMATION WINDOW. The previous revision required price to close
//      inside the PRZ *and* that exact bar to be an engulfing candle — one
//      bar satisfying two largely independent conditions. A PRZ visit lasts
//      only a few bars, and the odds any single one of them is also engulfing
//      are low, so the two rare events multiplied. Now the zone ARMS on entry
//      and stays armed for `confirmBars` bars, which is how §7.4's "a
//      confirmation while price is inside the PRZ" was always meant to read.
//   2. CANDIDATE ENUMERATION. The previous revision tested exactly one XABC
//      (the four most recent pivots). PRD §5.3 specifies enumerating over the
//      last N pivots. Now `maxCombos` sliding windows are tested per bar, so a
//      pattern whose C formed a few pivots back can still complete.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// HOW TO HISTORICALLY VALIDATE THIS SCRIPT (PRD §11.5)
//   1. Non-repainting: apply to a liquid chart (e.g. BTCUSDT, 1H), open Bar
//      Replay, step forward. A drawn polygon/PRZ box must NEVER disappear or
//      move on a later bar. Guaranteed structurally: ta.pivothigh/pivotlow
//      only return a value `pivotDepth` bars AFTER the pivot, once confirmed.
//   2. Case-study reproduction: load XAG/USD daily around the corrected PRD
//      §10.1 dates. Plotted B should print near 61.97 (78.6% of XA) and the
//      PRZ near 66.10 (1.270 XA) — NOT the source brief's incorrect 61.10 /
//      64.88-65.21. See the worked checks at the bottom of this file.
//   3. Strategy Tester: Performance Summary for net profit / win rate / PF,
//      List of Trades to cross-check fills against on-chart PRZ/stop/TP.
//      Commission (0.05%) and slippage (2 ticks) are fixed defaults in the
//      strategy() declaration — override from Properties -> "Commission and
//      slippage" to match your venue before drawing ANY conclusion (§7.2).
//   4. Gate verification: no trade's stop may sit inside the PRZ it entered
//      from, and every trade's R:R to TP2 must be >= rrMin. A violation is a
//      script defect, not a market outcome.
//
// SCOPE (PRD §1.6, §11 Phase 1): Gartley, Bat, Butterfly, Crab. One symbol,
// one timeframe, per chart — not the multi-symbol watchlist scanner or the
// manual-plotting mode (PRD §5.3, §8); Pine cannot provide either. Shark
// (5-point O-X-A-B-C, §3.3) is Phase 2 and not implemented here.
//
// TOLERANCE NOTE (PRD §1.6): tolPct is applied in ratio space to the B and C
// constraint windows for implementation simplicity — the common convention in
// public Pine harmonic scripts. The PRZ envelope itself IS computed the
// spec-faithful way: three contributor prices, then a single price-width
// tolerance band (tolPct% of |A-X|) around their min/max (§6.2).
// ============================================================================

//@version=6
// Commission/slippage are fixed defaults rather than script inputs — the
// strategy() declaration must be the first statement in the script, so it
// cannot reference input.*() variables declared elsewhere, and inlining
// input.*() calls as its argument values is unreliable across Pine Editor
// versions. Override both from Properties -> "Commission and slippage".
strategy("Harmonic PRZ Matrix — Gartley/Bat/Butterfly/Crab",
    shorttitle = "Harmonic PRZ",
    overlay = true,
    initial_capital = 10000,
    default_qty_type = strategy.fixed,
    default_qty_value = 1,
    pyramiding = 0,
    calc_on_every_tick = false,
    process_orders_on_close = true,
    commission_type = strategy.commission.percent,
    commission_value = 0.05,
    slippage = 2,
    max_lines_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- Inputs ---
grpDet = "Detection (§5)"
pivotDepth = input.int(5, "Pivot confirmation depth (bars each side)", minval = 2, group = grpDet, tooltip = "A pivot only becomes visible pivotDepth bars after it forms — this is what makes detection non-repainting (§5.2 D1/D2). Lower = more pivots, more candidates, more noise.")
maxPivots  = input.int(60, "Max stored zig-zag points", minval = 12, group = grpDet)
maxCombos  = input.int(3, "XABC windows tested per bar (§5.3)", minval = 1, maxval = 12, group = grpDet, tooltip = "1 tests only the four most recent pivots — that was the old behavior and it under-detects badly. Higher values slide the window back so a pattern whose C formed a few pivots ago can still complete. PRD §5.3 specifies enumeration; this is the bounded form of it.")
showCandidates = input.bool(true, "Show diagnostic dot on any partial B/C match", group = grpDet, tooltip = "Fires on the weak condition of B and C alone matching a pattern window — far more often than a full trade. Confirms the scanner is alive between setups.")
showPerfTable = input.bool(true, "Show on-chart performance table", group = grpDet, tooltip = "Per-pattern Zone/Trades/TP1/TP2/SL counts, live on the chart. A simplified parallel tracker (§7.2 caveats apply); the Strategy Tester remains authoritative for §11.5.")

grpPat = "Patterns (§3.2)"
useGartley   = input.bool(true, "Gartley",   group = grpPat)
useBat       = input.bool(true, "Bat",       group = grpPat)
useButterfly = input.bool(true, "Butterfly", group = grpPat)
useCrab      = input.bool(true, "Crab",      group = grpPat)

grpRisk = "Tolerance & Risk (§2.4, §7)"
tolPct         = input.float(2.0, "Ratio tolerance (%, ratio-space — see header)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = grpRisk)
rrMin          = input.float(2.0, "Minimum R:R to TP2 (§7.6 gate)", minval = 0.5, step = 0.1, group = grpRisk)
stopBufA       = input.float(0.05, "Extra stop buffer, in units of the §3.2 D-ratio", minval = 0.0, step = 0.01, group = grpRisk)
requireConfirm = input.bool(true, "Require a confirmation candle inside the PRZ (§7.4)", group = grpRisk, tooltip = "PRD §7.4: never rest a blind limit order at D. Turning this OFF enters on first PRZ touch — more trades, materially worse strategy, and contrary to the spec.")
confirmBars    = input.int(5, "Bars the PRZ stays armed awaiting confirmation", minval = 1, maxval = 50, group = grpRisk, tooltip = "Once price reaches the PRZ the zone ARMS for this many bars, during which a confirmation candle triggers entry. 1 reproduces the old (buggy) same-bar-only behavior. This is the single biggest driver of how many trades fire.")
useEngulfOnly  = input.bool(false, "Confirmation must be a full engulfing candle", group = grpRisk, tooltip = "OFF (default): a full engulfing OR a rejection/pin candle closing in the trade direction counts. ON: engulfing only — stricter, far fewer trades.")
riskPct        = input.float(1.0, "Risk % of equity per trade (§7.5)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = grpRisk)
useWickForZone = input.bool(true, "Zone touch counts on wick (not just close)", group = grpRisk, tooltip = "ON (default): the PRZ is considered reached if the bar's wick trades into it — which is what actually happens at a reversal zone. The ENTRY price is still the confirmation bar's close, so drawn levels always match the real fill. OFF: the bar must CLOSE inside the zone (PRD §6.4 strict reading) — more conservative, fewer arms.")

// ----------------------------------------------------------------- Types ---
type Pivot
    float price
    int   idx
    bool  isHigh

type PatternDef
    string name
    float  bLo
    float  bHi
    float  cLo
    float  cHi
    float  bcLo
    float  bcHi
    float  cdLo
    float  cdHi
    float  dLo
    float  dHi
    float  invalidR
    float  stopR
    color  col

// An armed PRZ: price has reached the zone and we are now waiting, for up to
// `confirmBars` bars, for a confirmation candle. Holds everything needed to
// compute the trade and draw the polygon at confirmation time.
type ArmedZone
    int   barsLeft
    bool  isBull
    float stopPrice
    float aPrice
    float invalidPrice
    float przLo
    float przHi
    int   xi
    float xp
    int   ai
    float ap
    int   bi
    float bp
    int   ci
    float cp

// ------------------------------------------------------------ Persisted ---
// Declared before the helpers below, because a Pine function reading a global
// var must see it declared earlier in the script — Pine does not hoist.
var Pivot[]      zz       = array.new<Pivot>()
var PatternDef[] defs     = array.new<PatternDef>()
var int[]        lastSigC = array.new<int>()

// Outcome tracker for the on-chart table. Purely observational — reads the
// same stop/tp1/tp2 a signal computed and watches later bars' high/low for a
// touch, entirely separate from strategy.entry/exit. It does NOT model
// commission/slippage or same-bar stop-vs-target ambiguity as precisely as
// the Strategy Tester (§7.2, §11.5); for a rigorous number use that tab.
var bool  tradeOpen       = false
var int   tradePatternIdx = -1
var float tradeStop       = na
var float tradeTp1        = na
var float tradeTp2        = na
var bool  tradeIsBullish  = false
var bool  tp1AlreadyHit   = false
var int[] cntTrades = array.new<int>()
var int[] cntTP1    = array.new<int>()
var int[] cntTP2    = array.new<int>()
var int[] cntSL     = array.new<int>()

// Funnel diagnostic: distinct candidates that reached the PRZ and armed,
// regardless of whether they ever confirmed. Zone minus Trades isolates how
// much the confirmation + R:R gate filters, separately from how often price
// reaches a valid PRZ at all.
var int[] lastZoneC = array.new<int>()
var int[] cntZone   = array.new<int>()

// One armed-zone slot per pattern. barsLeft > 0 means armed.
var ArmedZone[] armed = array.new<ArmedZone>()

// -------------------------------------------------------------- Helpers ---
inWindow(float val, float lo, float hi, float tol) =>
    val >= lo - tol and val <= hi + tol

// Confirmed, non-repainting zig-zag: only ever appends/replaces using
// ta.pivothigh/pivotlow output, which itself only resolves pivotDepth bars
// after the fact (§5.2 D1). Same-direction pivots collapse to the more
// extreme one; alternating pivots append, keeping X-A-B-C-D strictly
// alternating (§3.1 S1).
addPivot(float price, int idx, bool isHigh) =>
    n = array.size(zz)
    if n == 0
        array.push(zz, Pivot.new(price, idx, isHigh))
    else
        last = array.get(zz, n - 1)
        if last.isHigh == isHigh
            if (isHigh and price > last.price) or (not isHigh and price < last.price)
                array.set(zz, n - 1, Pivot.new(price, idx, isHigh))
        else
            array.push(zz, Pivot.new(price, idx, isHigh))
    if array.size(zz) > maxPivots
        array.shift(zz)

if barstate.isfirst
    if useGartley
        array.push(defs, PatternDef.new("Gartley",   0.618, 0.618, 0.382, 0.886, 1.130, 1.618, 1.000, 1.000, 0.786, 0.786, 1.000, 1.050, color.new(color.blue, 0)))
    if useBat
        array.push(defs, PatternDef.new("Bat",       0.382, 0.500, 0.382, 0.886, 1.618, 2.618, 1.270, 1.618, 0.886, 0.886, 1.000, 1.050, color.new(color.purple, 0)))
    if useButterfly
        array.push(defs, PatternDef.new("Butterfly", 0.786, 0.786, 0.382, 0.886, 1.618, 2.240, 1.270, 1.618, 1.270, 1.618, 1.618, 1.750, color.new(color.orange, 0)))
    if useCrab
        array.push(defs, PatternDef.new("Crab",      0.382, 0.618, 0.382, 0.886, 2.240, 3.618, 1.618, 1.618, 1.618, 1.618, 1.618, 1.902, color.new(color.red, 0)))
    // Guarded for the same reason as the loops below: with every pattern
    // disabled defs is empty, and Pine's `for 0 to -1` counts DOWNWARD — it
    // would push two phantom slots and desync `armed` from `defs`, which the
    // Stage 3 loop then reads out of bounds.
    if array.size(defs) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(defs) - 1
            array.push(lastSigC, -1)
            array.push(cntTrades, 0)
            array.push(cntTP1, 0)
            array.push(cntTP2, 0)
            array.push(cntSL, 0)
            array.push(lastZoneC, -1)
            array.push(cntZone, 0)
            array.push(armed, ArmedZone.new(0, false, na, na, na, na, na, 0, na, 0, na, 0, na, 0, na))

// ---------------------------------------------------------- Pivot feed  ---
ph = ta.pivothigh(pivotDepth, pivotDepth)
pl = ta.pivotlow(pivotDepth, pivotDepth)

if not na(ph)
    addPivot(ph, bar_index - pivotDepth, true)
if not na(pl)
    addPivot(pl, bar_index - pivotDepth, false)

// alertcondition/plotchar need plain series computed unconditionally every bar
var bool przActiveThisBar  = false
var bool anyShapeOkThisBar = false
przActiveThisBar  := false
anyShapeOkThisBar := false

// ------------------------------------- Stage 1+2: shape match, arm the zone ---
// Enumerates `maxCombos` sliding XABC windows (PRD §5.3). k=0 is the four most
// recent pivots; higher k slides the whole window one pivot further back, so a
// structure whose C formed a while ago can still complete now.
if array.size(defs) > 0
    n = array.size(zz)
    for k = 0 to maxCombos - 1
        if n >= 4 + k
            X = array.get(zz, n - 4 - k)
            A = array.get(zz, n - 3 - k)
            B = array.get(zz, n - 2 - k)
            C = array.get(zz, n - 1 - k)

            xaLeg = A.price - X.price   // §2.1 P(A,X,r) = A + r*(X-A); sign carries direction
            abLeg = A.price - B.price
            bcLeg = C.price - B.price

            if xaLeg != 0 and abLeg != 0 and bcLeg != 0
                isBullish = xaLeg > 0   // A>X: XA rises -> D projects down -> long at D (§2.3)

                // Only B and C are gated here (§2.2): both are fixed once C confirms
                // and don't depend on the still-forming D. BC-projection, AB=CD and
                // the D-of-XA ratio become contributor PRICES in the envelope below
                // (§6.1/§6.2); membership in that band is what gates D. That is the
                // spec-faithful PRZ: a convergence band, not three separate tests.
                bRatio = abLeg / xaLeg
                cRatio = bcLeg / abLeg
                validSide = bRatio > 0 and cRatio > 0

                for i = 0 to array.size(defs) - 1
                    pd = array.get(defs, i)
                    shapeOk = validSide and inWindow(bRatio, pd.bLo, pd.bHi, tolPct / 100) and inWindow(cRatio, pd.cLo, pd.cHi, tolPct / 100)
                    if shapeOk
                        anyShapeOkThisBar := true

                        // §6.1/§6.2 — PRZ envelope from three contributors
                        pXAlo = A.price + pd.dLo * (X.price - A.price)
                        pXAhi = A.price + pd.dHi * (X.price - A.price)
                        pBClo = C.price - pd.bcLo * bcLeg
                        pBChi = C.price - pd.bcHi * bcLeg
                        pCDlo = C.price - pd.cdLo * abLeg
                        pCDhi = C.price - pd.cdHi * abLeg
                        tolPrice = (tolPct / 100) * math.abs(xaLeg)

                        envLo = math.min(math.min(math.min(pXAlo, pXAhi), math.min(pBClo, pBChi)), math.min(pCDlo, pCDhi)) - tolPrice
                        envHi = math.max(math.max(math.max(pXAlo, pXAhi), math.max(pBClo, pBChi)), math.max(pCDlo, pCDhi)) + tolPrice
                        zLo = math.min(envLo, envHi)
                        zHi = math.max(envLo, envHi)

                        // Zone reached: wick-based by default (what actually happens at
                        // a reversal zone). Entry price is still the confirmation bar's
                        // close, so drawn levels always match the real fill.
                        touched = useWickForZone ? (low <= zHi and high >= zLo) : (close >= zLo and close <= zHi)

                        invalidPrice = A.price + pd.invalidR * (X.price - A.price)
                        refPrice = useWickForZone ? (isBullish ? low : high) : close
                        invalidBreached = isBullish ? refPrice < invalidPrice : refPrice > invalidPrice

                        az = array.get(armed, i)
                        if touched and not invalidBreached and az.barsLeft <= 0 and array.get(lastZoneC, i) != C.idx
                            array.set(lastZoneC, i, C.idx)
                            array.set(cntZone, i, array.get(cntZone, i) + 1)
                            przActiveThisBar := true

                            // §7.1 — stop ratio is per-pattern, never per trading-style
                            stopPx = A.price + (pd.stopR + stopBufA) * (X.price - A.price)

                            az.barsLeft     := confirmBars
                            az.isBull       := isBullish
                            az.stopPrice    := stopPx
                            az.aPrice       := A.price
                            az.invalidPrice := invalidPrice
                            az.przLo        := zLo
                            az.przHi        := zHi
                            az.xi           := X.idx
                            az.xp           := X.price
                            az.ai           := A.idx
                            az.ap           := A.price
                            az.bi           := B.idx
                            az.bp           := B.price
                            az.ci           := C.idx
                            az.cp           := C.price

                            box.new(C.idx, zHi, bar_index + confirmBars, zLo, xloc = xloc.bar_index, bgcolor = color.new(pd.col, 70), border_color = color.new(pd.col, 15), border_width = 2)

// ------------------------------- Stage 3+4: confirmation window, then entry ---
// Runs every bar over whatever is armed. A confirmation candle inside the
// window fires the trade; invalidation or an expired countdown disarms it.
// Guarded: with every pattern disabled the arrays are empty, and Pine's
// `for 0 to -1` counts DOWNWARD rather than skipping — an unguarded loop
// would read index -1 and throw at runtime.
if array.size(armed) > 0
    for i = 0 to array.size(armed) - 1
        az = array.get(armed, i)
        if az.barsLeft > 0
            pd = array.get(defs, i)
            breached = az.isBull ? low < az.invalidPrice : high > az.invalidPrice
            if breached
                az.barsLeft := 0
            else
                // Confirmation (§7.4). Full engulfing, or — unless useEngulfOnly
                // — a rejection candle: closes in the trade direction with a long
                // wick back out of the zone, which is the more common way a PRZ
                // actually reverses.
                rng = high - low
                bullEngulf = close > open and close[1] < open[1] and close >= open[1] and open <= close[1]
                bearEngulf = close < open and close[1] > open[1] and close <= open[1] and open >= close[1]
                bullPin = rng > 0 and close > open and (math.min(open, close) - low) / rng >= 0.5
                bearPin = rng > 0 and close < open and (high - math.max(open, close)) / rng >= 0.5
                bullOk = useEngulfOnly ? bullEngulf : (bullEngulf or bullPin)
                bearOk = useEngulfOnly ? bearEngulf : (bearEngulf or bearPin)
                confirmed = not requireConfirm or (az.isBull ? bullOk : bearOk)
                fired = false

                if confirmed and array.get(lastSigC, i) != az.ci
                    entryPrice = close                       // matches process_orders_on_close
                    adLeg = az.aPrice - entryPrice
                    tp1 = entryPrice + 0.382 * adLeg         // §7.3 — AD leg, not CD
                    tp2 = entryPrice + 0.618 * adLeg
                    risk = math.abs(entryPrice - az.stopPrice)
                    rr2 = risk > 0 ? math.abs(tp2 - entryPrice) / risk : 0.0

                    // §7.1 hard invariant: the stop must sit outside the PRZ it
                    // entered from, on the far side. Enforced, not assumed.
                    stopOutsidePrz = az.isBull ? az.stopPrice < az.przLo : az.stopPrice > az.przHi

                    if risk > 0 and rr2 >= rrMin and stopOutsidePrz   // §7.6 gates
                        fired := true
                        array.set(lastSigC, i, az.ci)
                        array.set(cntTrades, i, array.get(cntTrades, i) + 1)
                        if not tradeOpen
                            tradeOpen       := true
                            tradePatternIdx := i
                            tradeStop       := az.stopPrice
                            tradeTp1        := tp1
                            tradeTp2        := tp2
                            tradeIsBullish  := az.isBull
                            tp1AlreadyHit   := false

                        qty = (strategy.equity * riskPct / 100) / risk
                        entryId = pd.name + "_" + str.tostring(az.ci)
                        if az.isBull
                            strategy.entry(entryId, strategy.long, qty = qty)
                        else
                            strategy.entry(entryId, strategy.short, qty = qty)
                        strategy.exit(entryId + "_x1", from_entry = entryId, stop = az.stopPrice, limit = tp1, qty_percent = 50)
                        strategy.exit(entryId + "_x2", from_entry = entryId, stop = az.stopPrice, limit = tp2, qty_percent = 50)

                        line.new(az.xi, az.xp, az.ai, az.ap, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = pd.col, width = 2)
                        line.new(az.ai, az.ap, az.bi, az.bp, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = pd.col, width = 2)
                        line.new(az.bi, az.bp, az.ci, az.cp, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = pd.col, width = 2)
                        line.new(az.ci, az.cp, bar_index, entryPrice, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = pd.col, width = 2)

                        dirTxt = az.isBull ? "LONG" : "SHORT"
                        label.new(bar_index, entryPrice, text = pd.name + " " + dirTxt + "  R:R " + str.tostring(rr2, "#.##"), xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = az.isBull ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = pd.col, textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
                        alert(pd.name + " " + dirTxt + " confirmed — entry " + str.tostring(entryPrice) + " stop " + str.tostring(az.stopPrice) + " TP2 " + str.tostring(tp2) + " R:R " + str.tostring(rr2, "#.##"), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

                az.barsLeft := fired ? 0 : az.barsLeft - 1

// ------------------------------------------------- Outcome tracking (table) ---
// Watches the open tracked signal for a stop or target touch. Stop is checked
// first — if a bar spans both, it counts as a loss (pessimistic same-bar
// assumption, deliberately not flattering).
if tradeOpen
    hitStop = tradeIsBullish ? low <= tradeStop : high >= tradeStop
    if hitStop
        array.set(cntSL, tradePatternIdx, array.get(cntSL, tradePatternIdx) + 1)
        tradeOpen := false
    else
        hitTp1 = tradeIsBullish ? high >= tradeTp1 : low <= tradeTp1
        if hitTp1 and not tp1AlreadyHit
            tp1AlreadyHit := true
            array.set(cntTP1, tradePatternIdx, array.get(cntTP1, tradePatternIdx) + 1)
        hitTp2 = tradeIsBullish ? high >= tradeTp2 : low <= tradeTp2
        if hitTp2
            array.set(cntTP2, tradePatternIdx, array.get(cntTP2, tradePatternIdx) + 1)
            tradeOpen := false

// ------------------------------------------------------------ On-chart report ---
// Zone vs Trades is the funnel. Zone = candidates that reached the PRZ and
// armed. Trades = the subset that also confirmed and cleared the R:R gate.
// Zone near zero => price rarely reaches a valid PRZ (loosen tolPct, lower
// pivotDepth, raise maxCombos). Zone >> Trades => the confirmation/R:R gate
// is the bottleneck (raise confirmBars, or lower rrMin).
if showPerfTable and barstate.islast and array.size(defs) > 0
    var table perfTable = table.new(position.top_right, 7, array.size(defs) + 2, bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 15), border_width = 1, border_color = color.gray)
    hdrBg = color.new(color.gray, 50)
    table.cell(perfTable, 0, 0, "Pattern",    text_color = color.white, bgcolor = hdrBg)
    table.cell(perfTable, 1, 0, "Zone",       text_color = color.white, bgcolor = hdrBg)
    table.cell(perfTable, 2, 0, "Trades",     text_color = color.white, bgcolor = hdrBg)
    table.cell(perfTable, 3, 0, "TP1",        text_color = color.white, bgcolor = hdrBg)
    table.cell(perfTable, 4, 0, "TP2",        text_color = color.white, bgcolor = hdrBg)
    table.cell(perfTable, 5, 0, "SL",         text_color = color.white, bgcolor = hdrBg)
    table.cell(perfTable, 6, 0, "Win% (TP2)", text_color = color.white, bgcolor = hdrBg)

    totZone = 0
    totTrades = 0
    totTP1 = 0
    totTP2 = 0
    totSL = 0
    for i = 0 to array.size(defs) - 1
        pdRow = array.get(defs, i)
        z  = array.get(cntZone, i)
        t  = array.get(cntTrades, i)
        p1 = array.get(cntTP1, i)
        p2 = array.get(cntTP2, i)
        sl = array.get(cntSL, i)
        wr = t > 0 ? str.tostring(float(p2) / t * 100, "#.#") + "%" : "—"   // float() cast avoids int/int truncation
        table.cell(perfTable, 0, i + 1, pdRow.name, text_color = pdRow.col)
        table.cell(perfTable, 1, i + 1, str.tostring(z))
        table.cell(perfTable, 2, i + 1, str.tostring(t))
        table.cell(perfTable, 3, i + 1, str.tostring(p1))
        table.cell(perfTable, 4, i + 1, str.tostring(p2))
        table.cell(perfTable, 5, i + 1, str.tostring(sl))
        table.cell(perfTable, 6, i + 1, wr)
        totZone   := totZone + z
        totTrades := totTrades + t
        totTP1    := totTP1 + p1
        totTP2    := totTP2 + p2
        totSL     := totSL + sl

    lastRow = array.size(defs) + 1
    totWr = totTrades > 0 ? str.tostring(float(totTP2) / totTrades * 100, "#.#") + "%" : "—"
    table.cell(perfTable, 0, lastRow, "Total",                 text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(perfTable, 1, lastRow, str.tostring(totZone),   text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(perfTable, 2, lastRow, str.tostring(totTrades), text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(perfTable, 3, lastRow, str.tostring(totTP1),    text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(perfTable, 4, lastRow, str.tostring(totTP2),    text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(perfTable, 5, lastRow, str.tostring(totSL),     text_color = color.white)
    table.cell(perfTable, 6, lastRow, totWr,                   text_color = color.white)

alertcondition(przActiveThisBar, title = "PRZ Active", message = "Price entered a harmonic PRZ zone on {{ticker}} {{interval}}")

// Diagnostic only — NOT a trade signal. Fires when B and C alone match some
// enabled pattern's window. If this never appears, no candidate shape is
// forming at all: widen tolPct, lower pivotDepth, or raise maxCombos.
plotchar(showCandidates and anyShapeOkThisBar ? high : na, title = "Candidate B/C match (diagnostic, not a signal)", char = "•", location = location.abovebar, color = color.new(color.gray, 40), size = size.tiny)

// ============================================================================
// WORKED CHECKS — PRD §10, reproduced so the arithmetic above is auditable by
// hand against the same numbers the PRD verified independently in Python.
//
// Case Study 1 (corrected) — XAG/USD Bearish Butterfly
//   X=63.80  A=55.27  (xaLeg = A-X = -8.53, isBullish = false)
//   B near 61.97 -> bRatio = (A-B)/xaLeg = (55.27-61.97)/-8.53 = 0.786  [target 0.786]
//   D-of-XA at 1.270 -> A + 1.270*(X-A) = 55.27 + 1.270*8.53 = 66.10
//   stop = A + 1.750*(X-A) = 55.27 + 1.750*8.53 = 70.19  (beyond the 1.618 far edge)
//
// Case Study 2 (replacement) — BTC/USDT Bullish Bat
//   X=53500  A=71980  (xaLeg = A-X = 18480, isBullish = true)
//   D-of-XA at 0.886 -> A + 0.886*(X-A) = 71980 + 0.886*(53500-71980) = 55,607  [§10.2]
//   stop = A + 1.050*(X-A) = 71980 + 1.050*(-18480) = 52,576  (below X, non-zero gap)
// ============================================================================
